## Bias chain: noise at the bias nodes (typical, 27 C, 1.2 V)
| code | vbn noise uVrms 1k-1G | 1-1G | vbn LSB step mV | noise/LSB % (1k-1G) | vbp noise uVrms 1k-1G | 1-1G | vbp LSB step mV | noise/LSB % |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|

Integrated output noise of the bias nodes with the code held, from ngspice `.noise` (PSP thermal + flicker). "LSB step" is how far the node moves for one code step at that code; noise/LSB is the rms noise as a percentage of that step, i.e. how much of the 8-bit control the bias noise blurs.

